# shared/linux/desktops — desktop environments the optional GUI layer can bake
# (`make build … GUI=1 DE=<de>`). One token per line; '#' comments and blank
# lines ignored. A supported DE needs a branch per package family in
# shared/linux/scripts/gui-lib.sh. Not every distro × DE cell is buildable — the
# support matrix lives in shared/gui/README.md; an unbuildable cell fails
# loud at build time.
# Linux-only by construction: the darwin platform has no DE axis (its desktop is
# intrinsic), which is why there is no shared/darwin/desktops peer.
# Consumed by: Makefile (check-de), bin/tart-new (de validation; completion
# via completions/_tart-new), bin/lib/common.sh (base-image guard).
kde
gnome
xfce
